# GHSA-2mjx-qc3c-rqvc is rustls 0.23.36 compiled into @temporalio/core-bridge 1.24.0 and 1.25.0,
# the latest Temporal SDK release. SpaceApp reaches Temporal only over the private
# compose network without TLS (temporal:7233), so the TLS 1.3 handshake flaw has no
# reachable path. Remove once a Temporal SDK release ships rustls >= 0.23.45. Renewed from 2026-11-10 (Nous decision 2/11,
# CORE-002): no Temporal release ships a fixed rustls yet.
GHSA-2mjx-qc3c-rqvc exp:2026-12-01

# GHSA-c8m5-c952-6cm4 is the same rustls 0.23.36 in @temporalio/core-bridge 1.24.0 and 1.25.0 (fixed in 0.23.46): Debug formatting
# of a TLS session exposes its master secrets and resumption PSKs. SpaceApp reaches Temporal only over the private compose
# network without TLS (temporal:7233), so no rustls session exists to format. Remove with its sibling above, once a Temporal
# SDK release ships rustls >= 0.23.46. Renewed with its sibling until 2026-12-01.
GHSA-c8m5-c952-6cm4 exp:2026-12-01

# CVE-2026-118773 (glob 13.0.6, fixed in 14.0.2) and CVE-2026-118764 (minimatch 10.2.5, fixed in 11.0.1) are bundled inside
# npm 11.21.1, the newest npm 11 (it requires glob ^13 and minimatch ^10; npm 12 is a new major and is held). Both are denial
# of service from attacker-controlled glob patterns. In these images npm runs only on the image's own installs and the user's
# own packages in the CLI container, never on a pattern from the network. Swapping a major inside npm could break the CLI
# container's runtime installs. Remove once an npm 11 release bundles the fixed versions.
CVE-2026-118773 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-118764 exp:2026-12-01
